We need to expose Mimir Gateway internally through a LoadBalancer, then configure Alloy to remote_write to that internal address.

kubectl patch svc mimir-gateway \
  -n monitoring \
  -p '{
    "metadata": {
      "annotations": {
        "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type": "nlb",
        "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-scheme": "internal"
      }
    },
    "spec": {
      "type": "LoadBalancer"
    }
  }'


$ kubectl get svc -n monitoring | grep mimir-gateway
mimir-gateway                    LoadBalancer   172.20.200.43    a1a59c4d9dc284219ba4fd9ffd58cd12-1296e3666176ea98.elb.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com   80:30979/TCP,8080:30122/TCP   5h6m

Alloy
  ↓
prometheus.remote_write
  ↓
http://INTERNAL-MIMIR-NLB/api/v1/push

a1a59c4d9dc284219ba4fd9ffd58cd12-1296e3666176ea98.elb.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

